From 134790d09e1e3fe4b0c6355cdfb8aac47fbde6da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:06:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): resolve 2D area controls in an aligned setup

Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive refused any area control in
a setup that holds the part turned. Each world read of the area law
(picks, stitched chains, part material, silhouette, heights) already
goes through the setup frame, so the refusal is removed. The stock
outline stays furniture, as before.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/setup_align_2d_area.rs: an L part turned 90
degrees about Z cuts the same path as the part with the turn baked in,
keeps clear of the turned L, verifies with no gouge and posts.

Fixes #2210

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
